    "body": "Work landed locally on issue/79-radial-rapid-check (093b6fd), gating now:\n- **Why it was off**: M5.2 F2 switched the check off for Mode::Radial because the mill check reads stock as columns from above and saw a retract sliding out of its own sideways hole as a rapid through solid stock; the gate then trusted the cross-drill planner - blind.\n- **Now**: new `crates/sim/src/verify/rapids_radial.rs`. The drill's cutting length is modelled as discs square to the tool, sampled along each rapid with the controller's interpolated orientation, against the same stock the mill check uses; rapids may pass through material earlier cuts removed (retracts up a drilled hole, peck chip-breaks), but a rapid down a hole not yet drilled, or through uncut stock, blocks the post as `RapidInStock { at }`.\n- **It immediately caught a real one**: the drilling_cross fixture with a 44 mm box stock - the approach stops inside the box and the slide between holes passes through it. That is the #77 collision (fixed by PR #82, not yet on main). The test that wanted that fixture to run clean moved onto a bar-sized stock; a new test asserts any rapid inside the box is named and blocks the post.\n- Tests: radial_rapids (8, hand-made radial streams) + drilling_cross::a_rapid_inside_the_raw_box_stock_never_posts_silently.",
