    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T14:07:31Z",
    "body": "Review fixes landed locally (b8f1bad), gating now:\n- **Speed**: a 40-hole pecked radial program verified in ~9.5 s in debug; now ~0.25 s (cut cylinders built once with bounding boxes, a swept-box pre-filter scanned newest first, a stock bbox reject before point-in-region, one test for a disc wholly inside a drilled hole, no duplicate samples) - and the body step tightened from 1 mm to 0.5 mm. A wall-time test pins it.\n- **Deterministic app test** (`drilling_cross_rapids`): a hop spliced through the solid bar is named `RapidInStock` and `post_setup` refuses naming the rapid - independent of the #77 planner bug. It also found that the old box-stock test passed for the wrong reason (every post was blocked first by the test machine's missing B axis); both tests now load a mill-turn with a B trunnion and require the refusal to name the rapid.\n- **Edge tests**: past the bottom of a drilled hole, a graze within vs past the gouge tolerance, a half-in-hole diagonal retract.\n- **Fails closed**: a non-finite stock top/tolerance, an unusable tool radius or an axis with no direction convicts the rapids instead of passing silently; a zero flute reads as one diameter of body.\n- `drilling_cross.rs` 565 -> 252 lines (shared setup in `tests/cross_support`).",
